cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AI Queue Runner (AQR) or its verification data, please credit it as below and link to the repository."
title: "AI Queue Runner (AQR): a local task queue that runs coding work through Claude Code, Codex and Gemini CLI around usage limits"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jason
    alias: jasonwpgml
repository-code: "https://github.com/jasonwpgml/AQR"
url: "https://github.com/jasonwpgml/AQR"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
abstract: >-
  AI Queue Runner (AQR) is a Windows desktop app and headless worker, written
  in Python with PySide6 and SQLite, that queues coding tasks for AI coding
  agent CLIs (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex and Gemini CLI). It picks the next task
  by priority, dependencies, waiting time and per-agent availability, puts an
  agent into cooldown when its CLI reports a usage limit and resumes after the
  reset, reserves tasks atomically so no task runs twice, and can run
  conflicting tasks on the same repository in parallel git worktrees with
  optional auto-commit and draft pull requests. The repository includes a
  reproducible test and verification summary (CC BY 4.0).
keywords:
  - ai coding agents
  - task queue
  - scheduler
  - claude code
  - codex
  - gemini cli
  - git worktree
  - usage limits
  - rate limits
  - pyside6
  - sqlite
  - windows
